  "note": "前殿、丹房、账房 (native:niling/front, alchemy, counting; 逆灵宫 B): the hall with no idol — the long black table and the 逆灵天书 open on it, the iron burner, five 道士 on their cushions facing it, the 木鱼 by the one who leads, red lanterns lit by day, the shut north door to the 后殿 (C); the 丹房 west of it, soot-black, the three-legged 丹炉 burning blue in the middle, jar racks round the walls, the stone stair down in the south-west corner; the 账房 north of it, the 管事's great desk, ink everywhere. Old and used: wax on the table, ash before the burner, the cushions worn through, soot up the walls of the 丹房, ink on the 账房's floor.",
